## CS-011 — Shared conversation channel, simulator, and optional Meta test adapter

Status: Done
Owner: Codex
Date: 2026-07-18

Scope:
- Build the WhatsApp-compatible web simulator on the same patient-isolated conversation service used
  by the optional Meta WhatsApp Cloud API test adapter.
- Persist inbound and fixed system messages, expose ordered conversation history, and project at most
  one active extracted candidate for explicit confirmation.
- Support deterministic confirm, correct, and cancel commands without sending those commands back
  through GPT-5.6 or allowing a second extraction while confirmation is pending.
- Add webhook verification, signature verification, seeded sender mapping, provider-message
  idempotency, fixed outbound replies, and delivery-status updates for the optional Meta channel.
- Route separately approved clinician messages through Meta only after a mapped synthetic patient has
  entered through the Meta test channel; retain approval and record failure when delivery fails.

Validation:
- `.venv/bin/ruff check apps/api`: PASS.
- `.venv/bin/ruff format apps/api --check`: PASS, 45 files checked.
- `.venv/bin/pytest apps/api/tests`: PASS, 87 tests.
- Fresh SQLite `alembic upgrade head` and `alembic current`: PASS at `b5f7d11e04c2 (head)`.
- `npm run check:web`: PASS; 5 test files and 10 tests, lint, TypeScript, and production build.
- `npm run test:e2e -- --list`: PASS; the existing English Playwright story is discovered.
- Live Meta webhook and Graph API request: NOT RUN because no user-owned Meta credentials or public
  HTTPS callback are configured; no live-delivery or production-free claim is made.

Delivered:
- Patient-only conversation state, send, confirm, and cancel endpoints with strict role and patient
  isolation.
- Responsive `/patient/conversation` simulator with ordered bubbles, synthetic-data and emergency
  boundaries, an explicit **AI-extracted draft · not recorded** card, and confirmation controls.
- Shared conversation persistence for patient, fixed-template, and approved care-team messages while
  excluding system messages from the patient home care-team feed.
- A pending conversational candidate cannot create a reading, evaluation, or clinician task until an
  explicit patient confirmation runs the existing transactional reading and deterministic-rule path.
- Cancel/correct erases the unconfirmed raw message and extracted values; non-command text cannot
  replace an active candidate.
- Meta webhook GET challenge and POST HMAC validation, inbound text normalisation, digits-only
  sender-to-seeded-user mapping, unknown-sender non-disclosure, provider-ID deduplication, and delivery
  status recording.
- Server-only Graph API sender using configurable API version, phone-number ID, access token, verify
  token, app secret, and JSON phone map; no secret value is logged or returned.
- Approved clinician outbound delivery through the mapped Meta test channel with provider ID and
  audit metadata; simulator sends remain honestly marked as simulated.
- Environment templates and setup documentation that preserve the simulator fallback and require
  synthetic data only.

Notes:
- The browser conversation remains labelled **WhatsApp-compatible simulator** even when server-side
  Meta credentials exist; it never claims that browser messages travelled through WhatsApp.
- The Meta test adapter is implemented and provider-boundary tested with synthetic payloads and HMAC,
  but a live test still requires the user's Meta app, test recipient, token, app secret, and HTTPS URL.
- Meta account eligibility, token expiry, recipient restrictions, and production pricing are external
  constraints. The core demo does not depend on Meta approval or availability.
- GPT-5.6 extracts only. It does not diagnose, set priority, recommend treatment, change medication,
  override deterministic rules, or bypass confirmation.
- Fixed response text and translations are demonstration content and are not claimed to be clinically
  validated. All tests, numbers, identities, mappings, and webhook payloads are synthetic.

## CS-010 — Structured GPT-5.6 extraction and safe fallback

Status: Done
Owner: Codex
Date: 2026-07-18

Scope:
- Add the locked multilingual reading-extraction schema with strict integer types, forbidden extra
  fields, closed medication/context values, missing-field and ambiguity signals, and mandatory
  confirmation.
